Just to add some thoughts:

pendell@hotmail.com wrote:
> 1)  Have a light source or other way of seeing things at a distance. As
> I've said before,  the Light Shop is a guaranteed shop for a reason :).

If you don't have a lightsource, get off the dark levels ASAP. You can
search them later.

> 3) Just thought of this one: There are a fair number of cats and dogs
> in the mines. Save your tripe from Sokoban and make lots of pets. Let
> them wander the level and find all the traps. Better them than you :).
>

Pets are your friends regardless :) Keep them close, collect all the
tripe you find, and try every whistle you come across.

> 4) Stay out of melee if you can.  Most creatures can't kill what they
> can't touch.

The mines are an exception though, and at level 1 a hobbit or gnome
throwing daggers is a deadly situation. So do one (or both) of two
things:

Play a gnome to keep most of the mine denizens peaceful.

Stand on the upstairs, let them hurl daggers, pick up the daggers, go
upstairs, drop the daggers, heal,  go downstairs and repeat.

> 5) Engrave "E" to get a safe spot.

Make sure your safe spot is safe. Don't wait until you're cornered to
Engrave. Remember that while most monsters respect this trick,
projectiles don't. Engraving E in the mines can make you a pin cushion
in a few short turns.

